  breadcrumb={{
    items: [
      { name: "Home", url: "https://arthavi.com/" },
      { name: "Guides", url: "https://arthavi.com/guides/how-to-import-cas-cams-kfintech-nsdl/" },
      { name: "Import CAS", url: "https://arthavi.com/guides/how-to-import-cas-cams-kfintech-nsdl/" }
    ]
  }}
>

<main class="container">
  <section class="page-header fade-in" style="text-align: center; padding: 4rem 0 1.5rem; margin-top: 31px;">
    <h1>How to Import CAS from CAMS, KFintech & NSDL</h1>
  </section>

  <div class="aeo-answer-block fade-in" style="max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto 2rem; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 16px; background: rgba(99,102,241,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(99,102,241,0.2);">
    <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-body);">
      <strong style="color: var(--text-head);">To import your CAS, visit camsonline.com or kfintech.com, request a detailed CAS with your PAN, and upload the emailed PDF to Arthavi.</strong>
      The entire process takes under 5 minutes, and your complete mutual fund portfolio — every SIP, redemption, and dividend — appears instantly. No broker login required.
    </p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose fade-in delay-100" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">

    <h2>How to import CAS from CAMS</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Go to CAMS Online</strong> — Visit <a href="https://www.camsonline.com/Investors/Statements/Consolidated-Account-Statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">camsonline.com → CAS</a></li>
      <li><strong>Select "Detailed" statement</strong> — Choose "CAMS+KFintech" option to include all AMCs</li>
      <li><strong>Enter email and PAN</strong> — Use the email registered with your folios</li>
      <li><strong>Choose "Since Inception"</strong> — This gives your complete transaction history</li>
      <li><strong>Submit</strong> — CAS PDF arrives in your email within 2–5 minutes</li>
      <li><strong>Upload to Arthavi</strong> — Click "Import CAS", upload the PDF, enter your PAN as password</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>How to import CAS from KFintech</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Go to KFintech</strong> — Visit <a href="https://mfs.kfintech.com/investor/General/ConsolidatedAccountStatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mfs.kfintech.com → CAS</a></li>
      <li><strong>Select "Detailed" statement</strong> — Choose the transaction-level view</li>
      <li><strong>Enter PAN and email</strong> — Same as registered with your folios</li>
      <li><strong>Select date range</strong> — Use "Since Inception" for complete history</li>
      <li><strong>Submit and download</strong> — PDF arrives via email, password is your PAN</li>
      <li><strong>Upload to Arthavi</strong> — Same as CAMS: import, enter password, done</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>How to get CAS from NSDL (for demat mutual funds)</h2>
    <p>If your mutual funds are held in <strong>demat mode</strong> (through your depository participant), request CAS from NSDL:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Visit <a href="https://nsdl.co.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nsdl.co.in</a> → Investor Services → CAS</li>
      <li>Enter your DP ID and Client ID</li>
      <li>Download the generated CAS PDF</li>
    </ol>
    <p><strong>Note:</strong> Most retail investors hold mutual funds in "statement mode" (non-demat), so CAMS/KFintech CAS covers 95%+ of holdings. NSDL CAS is only needed for demat-held mutual fund units.</p>

    <h2>Why is my CAS not showing all mutual funds?</h2>
    <p>Common reasons:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Different email addresses</strong> — Some funds may be registered under a different email. Try requesting with PAN only.</li>
      <li><strong>Demat-held funds</strong> — Funds bought via Zerodha/Groww in demat mode won't appear in CAMS/KFintech CAS. Use NSDL CAS for those.</li>
      <li><strong>Closed folios</strong> — Fully redeemed funds may not appear in a "current holdings" view. Request "since inception" detailed statement.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Can Arthavi parse password-protected CAS files?</h2>
    <p>Yes. When you upload your CAS, Arthavi asks for the password (your PAN). The PDF is decrypted <strong>locally in your browser</strong> — the password never reaches Arthavi's servers. This is a critical privacy measure that sets Arthavi apart from trackers that require email access.</p>

    <div style="text-align: center; margin: 3rem 0;">
      <a href="https://app.arthavi.com/demo" class="btn btn-demo" style="padding: 1rem 2.5rem; font-size: 1.1rem;">
        Try Arthavi Demo — No Signup Required
      </a>
      <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-muted);">No broker login. No spam calls. Your data stays yours.</p>
    </div>

    <section id="faq" style="margin-top: 3rem;">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>How to import CAS from CAMS to a portfolio tracker?</h3>
      <p>Visit camsonline.com, request detailed CAS with PAN and email, receive via email, upload to Arthavi. Takes under 5 minutes.</p>
      <h3>How to get CAS from KFintech?</h3>
      <p>Visit kfintech.com → CAS, enter PAN and email, select "Detailed", submit. PDF arrives in minutes.</p>
      <h3>What is the CAS password?</h3>
      <p>Your PAN number in uppercase (e.g., ABCDE1234F).</p>
      <h3>Why is my CAS not showing all mutual funds?</h3>
      <p>Check if funds are under different email or held in demat mode (use NSDL CAS for demat).</p>
      <h3>Can Arthavi parse password-protected CAS files?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Password decryption happens in your browser — PAN never reaches our servers.</p>
    </section>

    <nav style="margin-top: 3rem; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 16px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);">
